---
functor: 1
title: All set rules
---

set heading(numbering: none)

A `set` line changes the look of the whole document. Write it on its own line, before the text it changes.

| Rule | Option | Default |
|:--|:--|:--|
| `set vec(...)` | `style` | `arrow` |
| `set vec(...)` | `fence` | `paren` |
| `set vec(...)` | `body` | `column` |
| `set vec(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set vec(...)` | `inline` | `small` |
| `set mat(...)` | `fence` | `paren` |
| `set mat(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set mat(...)` | `inline` | `small` |
| `set cases(...)` | `fence` | `brace.left` |
| `set cases(...)` | `word` | `none` |
| `set cases(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set binom(...)` | `fence` | `paren` |
| `set binom(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set abs(...)` | `fence` | `vbar` |
| `set abs(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set norm(...)` | `fence` | `vbar.x2` |
| `set norm(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set inner(...)` | `fence` | `angle` |
| `set inner(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set floor(...)` | `fence` | `floor` |
| `set floor(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set ceil(...)` | `fence` | `ceil` |
| `set ceil(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set wrap(...)` | `grow` | `stretch` |
| `set diagram(...)` | `gap` | `normal` |
| `set diagram(...)` | `inline` | `small` |
| `set diagram(...)` | `cross` | `gap` |
| `set dd(...)` | `style` | `italic` |
| `set document(...)` | `style` | `quiet` |
| `set document(...)` | `accent` | `none` |
| `set heading(...)` | `numbering` | `on` |
| `set page(...)` | `size` | `a4` |
| `set page(...)` | `margin` | `2.5cm` |
| `set text(...)` | `size` | `11pt` |
| `set text(...)` | `font` | `Functor LM` |

A `fence` value is a fence operation such as `brack` or `vbar.x2`, the word `none`, or any one symbol, for example a `sym`. A `grow` value is `stretch` or `magnify`.
